    </item>
    <item>
      <title>USS Bulkeley Participates in Mavi Balina 2026</title>
      <link>https://www.navy.mil/Press-Office/News-Stories/display-news/Article/4655461/uss-bulkeley-participates-in-mavi-balina-2026/</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Arleigh Burke-class guided-missile destroyer USS Bulkeley (DDG 84) participated in Turkish-led exercise Mavi Balina 2026 in the Eastern Mediterranean Sea Nov. 9-20.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;img src='https://media.defense.gov/2026/Nov/20/2004034369/150/150/0/261113-N-EE352-2278.JPG' alt='Turkish Navy SH-70 helicopters fly in formation past Arleigh Burke-class guided-missile destroyer USS Bulkeley (DDG 84) during a photo exercise as part of Exercise Mavi Balina in the Mediterranean Sea, Nov. 13, 2026. Mavi Balina is an international anti-submarine warfare exercise led by Turkish Naval Forces to provide realistic operational training in surface and submarine warfare and promote friendship, mutual understanding and cooperation. Bulkeley is a forward-deployed naval asset assigned to the U.S. 6th Fleet area of operations to support the warfighting effectiveness, lethality and readiness of U.S. Naval Forces Europe-Africa and defend U.S., Allied and partner interests in the region. (U.S. Navy photo by Mass Communication Specialist 2nd Class Leon Vonguyen)' /&gt; &lt;br /&gt;
</description>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:26:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>U.S. 6th Fleet Public Affairs</dc:creator>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.navy.mil/Press-Office/News-Stories/display-news/Article/4655461/uss-bulkeley-participates-in-mavi-balina-2026/</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://media.defense.gov/2026/Nov/20/2004034369/600/400/0/261113-N-EE352-2278.JPG" type="image/jpeg" />
      <category>All Navy Categories</category>
      <category>Navy Headlines</category>
