    <item>
      <title>USS North Dakota (SSN 784) Changes Homeport to Pearl Harbor</title>
      <link>https://www.navy.mil/Press-Office/News-Stories/display-news/Article/4648979/uss-north-dakota-ssn-784-changes-homeport-to-pearl-harbor/</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Virginia-class fast-attack submarine USS North Dakota (SSN 784) arrived at its new home port of Pearl Harbor, Hawaii, Nov. 13, 2026. North Dakota completed an Extended Drydocking Selected Restricted Availability at Portsmouth Naval Shipyard, in Kittery, Maine, before joining Submarine Squadron 1 as its sixth Virginia-class fast-attack submarine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;img src='https://media.defense.gov/2026/Nov/13/2004027416/150/150/0/261113-N-DZ831-1719.JPG' alt='Virginia-class fast-attack submarine USS North Dakota (SSN 784) maneuvers as it arrives to Joint Base Pearl Harbor-Hickam during its change of homeport, Nov. 13, 2026. North Dakota is assigned to Submarine Squadron 1 and is capable of supporting various missions, including anti-submarine warfare, anti-surface ship warfare, strike warfare, special operations forces support, and intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance. (U.S. Navy photo by Chief Mass Communication Specialist Omar A. Dominquez)' /&gt; &lt;br /&gt;
</description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:50:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Lt.j.g. Samantha Prewitt, Commander, Submarine Force, U.S. Pacific Fleet Public Affairs</dc:creator>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.navy.mil/Press-Office/News-Stories/display-news/Article/4648979/uss-north-dakota-ssn-784-changes-homeport-to-pearl-harbor/</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://media.defense.gov/2026/Nov/13/2004027416/600/400/0/261113-N-DZ831-1719.JPG" type="image/jpeg" />
